      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Fix truncate length bound and verify",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "# Objective\nFix truncate(text, max) in src/text.js so it never returns more than max characters, and ends in ... when it had to cut. Leave capitalize and all other behaviour untouched.\n\n# Work\n1. Change the cut branch to reserve room for the ellipsis: text.slice(0, Math.max(0, max - 3)) + ... and handle max < 3 sensibly.\n2. Add tests covering a cut case and the length bound.\n3. Run npm test and serve / for the preview capture.\n\n# Acceptance\n- Result length <= max for any input.\n- Cut result ends in ...\n- No change to non-truncated pass-through or capitalize.\n- Existing tests pass.",
